# Build context for the sandbox image is the MONOREPO ROOT (for the source-copied bits: skills, bin scripts,
# entrypoint, connectors). The compiled payload does NOT ride this context — prepare-image-trees.sh
# assembles it in .image-out/, which enters the build as the separate named context `trees` (its node_modules
# and dist are needed there; the excludes below don't apply to a named context).
.image-out
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/dist
**/dist-bin
**/dist-*
**/deploy
**/generated
**/.astro
**/out-tsc
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Rust build output (ic, netd, the desktop app): ~16 GB on a dev machine that no COPY reads, and BuildKit uploads the
# whole context before the first COPY (162 s measured on rog, 2026-11-19). netd builds from its own context.
**/target
# The workspace's own sandbox config and records, never an image input.
.intentic
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
_tools/localhost-https
.demo
desired-state
intent
test
